# Queue Audit Skill - Kiểm Toán Message Queue Toàn Diện

## Tổng quan

Message queue là critical infrastructure cho asynchronous processing, event-driven architecture, và microservices communication. Skill này cung cấp framework để audit queue implementation, ensure reliability, và optimize performance.

## Purpose (Mục đích)

Queue Audit Skill được thiết kế để:

1. **Architecture Review**: Evaluate queue design và patterns
2. **Reliability Assessment**: Ensure message delivery guarantees
3. **Performance Analysis**: Identify bottlenecks và optimization opportunities
4. **Error Handling**: Review dead letter và retry mechanisms
5. **Monitoring Setup**: Establish queue observability

### Khi nào sử dụng Queue Audit

- Khi investigating message loss
- Khi processing delays observed
- Khi consumer backlog growing
- Khi planning new queue implementation
- Khi scaling considerations
- Khi debugging intermittent failures

## Input (Đầu vào)

- [ ] Queue configuration (exchanges, queues, bindings)
- [ ] Message schemas
- [ ] Consumer implementations
- [ ] Dead letter queue setup
- [ ] Monitoring metrics
- [ ] Error logs
- [ ] Retry configurations

## Output (Đầu ra)

- [ ] Queue architecture diagram
- [ ] Reliability assessment
- [ ] Performance bottlenecks
- [ ] Recommended improvements
- [ ] Monitoring setup
- [ ] Migration plan (nếu cần)

## Workflow (Quy trình)

### Phase 1: Architecture Analysis

### Bước 1: Queue Topology Review

```typescript
// RabbitMQ Topology Analysis
interface QueueTopology {
  exchanges: Exchange[];
  queues: Queue[];
  bindings: Binding[];
  deadLetterExchange?: string;
}

interface Exchange {
  name: string;
  type: 'direct' | 'fanout' | 'topic' | 'headers';
  durable: boolean;
  bindings: string[];
}

interface Queue {
  name: string;
  durable: boolean;
  autoDelete: boolean;
  arguments: {
    xDeadLetterExchange?: string;
    xDeadLetterRoutingKey?: string;
    xMessageTTL?: number;
    xMaxLength?: number;
  };
  consumers: number;
  messages: number;
}

async function analyzeQueueTopology(): Promise<QueueTopology> {
  const connections = await getRabbitMQConnections();
  
  return {
    exchanges: await listExchanges(),
    queues: await listQueues(),
    bindings: await listBindings(),
    deadLetterExchange: 'dlx.exchange'
  };
}
```

### Bước 2: Message Flow Analysis

```typescript
// Message Flow Tracking
interface MessageFlow {
  exchange: string;
  routingKey: string;
  queue: string;
  consumer: string;
  avgProcessingTime: number;
  errorRate: number;
  throughput: number;
}

async function analyzeMessageFlows(): Promise<MessageFlow[]> {
  const flows: MessageFlow[] = [];
  const queues = await listQueues();
  
  for (const queue of queues) {
    const stats = await getQueueStats(queue.name);
    
    flows.push({
      exchange: queue.exchange,
      routingKey: queue.routingKey,
      queue: queue.name,
      consumer: queue.consumerTag,
      avgProcessingTime: stats.ack_time - stats.delivery_time,
      errorRate: stats.error_count / stats.total_count,
      throughput: stats.total_count / stats.window_seconds
    });
  }
  
  return flows;
}
```

### Phase 2: Reliability Assessment

### Bước 3: Delivery Guarantee Analysis

```typescript
// RabbitMQ: Publisher confirms
async function publishWithConfirms(channel: Channel, msg: Message): Promise<void> {
  const confirm = await channel.publish(
    'exchange.name',
    'routing.key',
    Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(msg)),
    {
      persistent: true,  // Message survives broker restart
      deliveryMode: 2,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      messageId: generateUUID(),
      timestamp: Date.now()
    }
  );
  
  if (!confirm) {
    throw new Error('Message was not confirmed by broker');
  }
}

// Kafka: Exactly-once semantics
const producer = kafka.producer({
  enableIdempotence: true,
  acks: 'all',
  retries: 3,
  maxInFlightRequests: 5
});

await producer.send({
  topic: 'orders',
  messages: [{
    key: orderId,
    value: JSON.stringify(orderEvent),
    headers: {
      'correlation-id': correlationId
    }
  }]
});
```

### Bước 4: Consumer Implementation Review

```typescript
// Reliable Consumer Pattern
class ReliableConsumer {
  private readonly maxRetries = 3;
  private readonly retryDelay = 5000;
  
  async processMessage(msg: Message): Promise<void> {
    const attempt = msg.headers['x-retry-count'] || 0;
    
    try {
      await this.executeHandler(msg);
      await this.acknowledge(msg);
    } catch (error) {
      if (attempt < this.maxRetries) {
        await this.retry(msg, attempt + 1);
      } else {
        await this.sendToDeadLetter(msg, error);
      }
    }
  }
  
  private async retry(msg: Message, attempt: number): Promise<void> {
    // Reject and requeue with delay
    await this.channel.nack(msg, false, false);
    
    // Wait before retry
    await sleep(this.retryDelay * attempt);
    
    // Republish with retry count
    await this.channel.publish(
      'retry.exchange',
      msg.fields.routingKey,
      msg.content,
      {
        headers: { 'x-retry-count': attempt }
      }
    );
  }
  
  private async sendToDeadLetter(msg: Message, error: Error): Promise<void> {
    await this.channel.publish(
      'dlx.exchange',
      'dlq.routing',
      msg.content,
      {
        headers: {
          'x-original-routing-key': msg.fields.routingKey,
          'x-death-reason': error.message,
          'x-failed-at': new Date().toISOString()
        }
      }
    );
    
    await this.acknowledge(msg);
  }
}

// BullMQ: Job processing with retries
const orderProcessor = new Worker('orders', async (job) => {
  if (job.attemptsMade < job.opts.retries) {
    throw new Error('Temporary failure');
  }
  
  return processOrder(job.data);
}, {
  connection: redisConnection,
  limiter: {
    max: 10,
    duration: 1000
  },
  defaultJobOptions: {
    attempts: 3,
    backoff: {
      type: 'exponential',
      delay: 2000
    },
    removeOnComplete: 100,
    removeOnFail: 1000
  }
});

orderProcessor.on('failed', (job, err) => {
  logger.error('Order processing failed', {
    jobId: job.id,
    attempts: job.attemptsMade,
    error: err.message
  });
});
```

### Phase 3: Performance Optimization

### Bước 5: Consumer Scaling

```typescript
// Auto-scaling consumers based on queue depth
class ScalingConsumerManager {
  private consumers: Map<string, number> = new Map();
  private readonly minConsumers = 1;
  private readonly maxConsumers = 10;
  private readonly scaleUpThreshold = 100;
  private readonly scaleDownThreshold = 10;
  
  async monitorAndScale() {
    const queues = await this.getMonitoredQueues();
    
    for (const queue of queues) {
      const depth = await this.getQueueDepth(queue.name);
      const currentConsumers = this.consumers.get(queue.name) || this.minConsumers;
      
      if (depth > this.scaleUpThreshold && currentConsumers < this.maxConsumers) {
        await this.scaleUp(queue.name);
      } else if (depth < this.scaleDownThreshold && currentConsumers > this.minConsumers) {
        await this.scaleDown(queue.name);
      }
    }
  }
  
  private async scaleUp(queueName: string) {
    const current = this.consumers.get(queueName) || 0;
    this.consumers.set(queueName, current + 1);
    
    await this.createConsumer(queueName, `consumer-${Date.now()}`);
    logger.info('Scaled up consumer', { queue: queueName, count: current + 1 });
  }
}
```

### Bước 6: Batch Processing

```typescript
// Kafka: Batch consumer
const consumer = kafka.consumer({
  groupId: 'order-processor',
  maxBytes: 1048576, // 1MB per batch
  maxWaitTimeInMs: 5000
});

await consumer.subscribe({ topic: 'orders', fromBeginning: false });

await consumer.run({
  eachBatchAutoResolve: false,
  eachBatch: async ({ batch, heartbeat, resolveOffset, commitOffsetsIfNecessary }) => {
    const messages = batch.messages;
    
    // Batch process
    const orders = messages.map(m => JSON.parse(m.value.toString()));
    const results = await processOrdersBatch(orders);
    
    // Mark progress
    for (const result of results) {
      resolveOffset(result.offset);
      await heartbeat();
    }
    
    // Commit offsets
    await commitOffsetsIfNecessary();
  }
});

// RabbitMQ: Consumer with prefetch
await channel.prefetch(10); // Process 10 messages at a time

channel.consume('orders', async (msg) => {
  if (msg) {
    try {
      await processOrder(JSON.parse(msg.content.toString()));
      channel.ack(msg);
    } catch (error) {
      channel.nack(msg, false, true); // Requeue
    }
  }
});
```

